      "math_academy_id": "q-146182",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}, & \\,x=1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}, & \\,x=3 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ is shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=4] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+3\\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
